# Textus Knowledge Workbench CML Model

> NOTE FOR CODEX
>
> Canonical CML source location. Replace this scaffold with valid current CML only after inspecting Cozy/CML grammar and representative models.
>
> Design sources:
> - docs/notes/architecture.md
> - docs/journal/2026-09-23-knowledge-workbench-establishment.md
> - docs/phase/phase-1.md
>
> Primary application use case:
> - Form, review and admit Information from a raw/prepared Information Candidate.
>
> Model Use Case and Application Workflow separately where supported.
>
> Phase 1 workflow:
> Register Candidate
> -> Resolve Evidence / Context
> -> Edit / Correct
> -> Semantic Grounding / Mapping
> -> Human Review
> -> Approve / Hold / Reject
> -> Request KnowledgeHub Information Admission
> -> retain Admission Trace.
>
> Candidate sources:
> - TKL PreparedMaterial / raw candidate
> - NICT Editing Studio confirmed capture-derived raw data
>
> Important boundaries:
> - TKW owns Information Candidate lifecycle and human admission workflow.
> - TKL owns evidence federation/preparation.
> - Editing Studio owns publishing/editorial domain interaction and views.
> - Mobile Capture Confirm authorizes transfer only.
> - KnowledgeHub owns canonical Information processing/runtime/storage.
> - KnowledgeProjection maps canonical Information to RDF/Open Knowledge downstream.
> - AI cannot perform final Information Admission.
> - Reuse CNCF/KnowledgeHub canonical types where semantics match.
>
